# HAMSTYLE :: size :: one_col -- 1-column journal figure
# 3.37 in = single column of a two-column APS/AIP page (86 mm). This is the size
# hamStyle.mplstyle already carries; the file exists so hamhelper.install can
# switch back to it.
# Type: ticks and legend 9 pt, axis labels and titles 10 pt. Set from publisher
# guidance (IOP asks 8-12 pt at final size; APS asks lettering at least 2 mm
# high, which is 8.5 pt of Times; Nature allows 5-7 pt of Arial) and from the
# rule that a figure's type should not be smaller than its caption.
# 7 pt Times digits are only 1.7 mm high, under the APS floor.
# Draw at final width, place at 100%, never let the copy editor rescale.
figure.figsize:         3.37, 2.40
font.size:              9.0
axes.titlesize:         10.0
axes.labelsize:         10.0
xtick.labelsize:        9.0
ytick.labelsize:        9.0
legend.fontsize:        9.0
axes.linewidth:         0.75
axes.labelpad:          2.5
axes.titlepad:          3.5
lines.linewidth:        1.3
lines.markersize:       3.2
grid.linewidth:         0.45
errorbar.capsize:       1.3
xtick.major.size:       3.3
ytick.major.size:       3.3
xtick.minor.size:       1.8
ytick.minor.size:       1.8
xtick.major.width:      0.75
ytick.major.width:      0.75
xtick.minor.width:      0.6
ytick.minor.width:      0.6
xtick.major.pad:        2.8
ytick.major.pad:        2.8
legend.handlelength:    1.7
